@startuml everyday-ticket-classification
title Intake classification of an everyday ticket (ADR-052)

participant "IncidentIntakePipeline" as P
participant "CompositeClassifier" as C
participant "KeywordClassifier" as K
participant "NaiveBayesClassifier" as N
participant "ServiceMatcher" as S
participant "ServiceCorroboration" as SC
participant "TicketRouter" as R

P -> C : classify(title, description)
C -> K : classify (distinct terms, pair terms, tie, security flag)
K --> C : category, support per category
alt keywords confident (>= 0.85) and no security term for another category
  C --> P : keyword result
else
  C -> N : classify
  N --> C : category, confidence
  note over C
    1. title-led tie: Naive Bayes may not break a tie against the title
    2. decisive keywords (>= 2 terms, clear lead) beat an unsupported Naive Bayes answer
    3. a capped ticket keeps the keyword label when no keyword supports Naive Bayes
    4. otherwise the ADR-034 caps (0.55) apply; a security term caps a ticket another category wins
  end note
  C --> P : result (carries keyword support and security flag)
end
P -> S : findBestMatch(title, description, services)
S --> P : matched IT service (or none)
P -> R : owningTeamId(category, null)
R --> P : team that handles the category
P -> SC : apply(result, service, team)
note right of SC
  lifts a capped ticket to exactly 0.60 only if
  a keyword supports the category AND the service
  (not the general one) is owned by that team AND
  there is no security indicator
end note
SC --> P : result
alt confidence >= 0.60
  P -> P : save, then assign (TicketDispatchService)
else
  P -> P : needsTriage, administrator decides
end
@enduml
